      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "With the discovery of master buffer one triggers buffering improperly (https://vrchat.canny.io/bug-reports/p/masterbufferone-buffers-when-non-masters-initiate-the-trigger) and other buffering triggers seemingly failing, this feature request would make it much easier to debug triggers in maps. Not only should we see other users broadcasted triggers, the log should also show what buffered triggers are firing.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-16T08:35:33.982Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In the old logs, we could see when a trigger caused an RPC. This was very useful for debugging triggers. With the recent log update, it is no longer as easy to see when a trigger is sent as an RPC or who initiated the trigger. \nCan you please add a log statement to say when something is sent over the network (outgoing and incoming) and which user initiated the trigger?",
